WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:06.741
When Sir Richard left Sherwood Forest, he didn't travel alone.

2
00:00:06.742 --> 00:00:09.934
A group of Robin's men went with him.

3
00:00:09.935 --> 00:00:17.843
The group headed along a straight highway toward the monastery, so that Sir Richard could pay his debt to Abbot Vincent.

4
00:00:17.844 --> 00:00:25.303
Far away in the distance rose the towers of the abbey, with tall trees surrounding it.

5
00:00:25.304 --> 00:00:30.289
Meanwhile, inside the abbey, the abbot was holding a big feast.

6
00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:37.770
He wore soft robes of fine silk, a black velvet cap, and a heavy gold chain around his neck.

7
00:00:37.771 --> 00:00:43.028
While he ate, a falcon sat on the arm of his large chair.

8
00:00:43.029 --> 00:00:47.323
The Sheriff of Nottingham sat on one side of the abbot.

9
00:00:47.324 --> 00:00:50.730
His purple robe was trimmed with fur.

10
00:00:50.731 --> 00:00:53.969
A famous judge sat on the other side of the abbot.

11
00:00:53.970 --> 00:00:58.196
The judge's clothes were dark and plain, but he was quite happy.

12
00:00:58.197 --> 00:01:04.258
The abbot had just paid him eighty gold coins for helping to ruin Sir Richard.

13
00:01:04.259 --> 00:01:10.872
"Are you sure you'll get Sir Richard's castle and all his land?" the sheriff asked the abbot.

14
00:01:10.873 --> 00:01:16.260
"Oh, yes," said Abbot Vincent with a sinister smile.

15
00:01:16.261 --> 00:01:18.897
He took a long drink of wine.

16
00:01:18.898 --> 00:01:23.339
"Sir Richard doesn't know I've been watching him closely.

17
00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:27.610
He has no money to pay his debt."

18
00:01:27.611 --> 00:01:33.845
Suddenly there came the sound of a horse's hooves clattering as it entered the courtyard below.

19
00:01:33.846 --> 00:01:38.498
"See who that is!" the abbot commanded a servant.

20
00:01:38.499 --> 00:01:40.849
The servant looked out the window.

21
00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:43.547
"It's a knight with some men.

22
00:01:43.548 --> 00:01:51.391
The knight is dressed plainly, but the men are well armed with bows and arrows."

23
00:01:51.392 --> 00:01:55.281
"That must be Sir Richard," said the abbot.

24
00:01:55.282 --> 00:01:58.432
"But why has he brought so many men?"

25
00:01:58.433 --> 00:02:01.222
The judge was suddenly nervous.

26
00:02:01.223 --> 00:02:07.202
"Will he attack us? Abbot, maybe you should give him more time to pay his debt."

27
00:02:07.203 --> 00:02:10.293
"Don't worry," scoffed the abbot.

28
00:02:10.294 --> 00:02:15.979
"This knight is very gentle. He won't hurt anyone."

29
00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:18.505
Just then the door swung open.

30
00:02:18.506 --> 00:02:24.289
Sir Richard entered the room with his hands folded and his head bowed humbly.

31
00:02:24.290 --> 00:02:27.327
His men waited by the door with their weapons.

32
00:02:27.328 --> 00:02:33.121
The knight approached the table and knelt on one knee in front of Abbot Vincent.

33
00:02:33.122 --> 00:02:37.005
"Where's my money?" demanded the abbot.

34
00:02:37.006 --> 00:02:39.794
Sir Richard's cheeks turned red.

35
00:02:39.795 --> 00:02:43.259
"Please show me some mercy," he said softly.

36
00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:45.530
"I don't have any money."

37
00:02:45.531 --> 00:02:49.230
Abbot Vincent said nothing, but he looked angry.

38
00:02:49.231 --> 00:02:52.053
Sir Richard appealed to the judge.

39
00:02:52.054 --> 00:02:55.337
"Please, sir, can you help me?"

40
00:02:55.338 --> 00:03:00.852
The abbot was right—this quiet knight didn't seem threatening at all.

41
00:03:00.853 --> 00:03:07.873
So the judge boldly said, "The money is due today. You must pay it now!"

42
00:03:07.874 --> 00:03:11.270
Sir Richard was not ready to give up.

43
00:03:11.271 --> 00:03:15.260
"What about you, Sheriff? Can you help me?"

44
00:03:15.261 --> 00:03:19.213
"This really is no business of mine, but I'll do what I can."

45
00:03:19.214 --> 00:03:27.209
The sheriff nudged the abbot with a knee and whispered, "Can you reduce the amount the knight owes you?"

46
00:03:27.210 --> 00:03:31.548
"All right," muttered the abbot to Sir Richard.

47
00:03:31.549 --> 00:03:38.260
"Give me three hundred pounds, Sir Richard, and I'll consider your debt paid."

48
00:03:38.261 --> 00:03:40.152
Sir Richard shook his head.

49
00:03:40.153 --> 00:03:44.127
"I'm sorry, but I can't pay three hundred pounds now, Abbot.

50
00:03:44.128 --> 00:03:46.829
Please give me another year to pay my debt."

51
00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:51.360
"Not another day!" Abbot Vincent said sternly.

52
00:03:51.361 --> 00:03:56.699
"Either pay it today or everything you own is mine."

53
00:03:56.700 --> 00:03:58.451
Sir Richard stood up.

54
00:03:58.452 --> 00:04:02.222
The gentle knight suddenly looked stern and furious.

55
00:04:02.223 --> 00:04:05.624
"I've tried to be polite to you!" he snapped.

56
00:04:05.625 --> 00:04:08.716
"But you haven't even offered me anything to eat.

57
00:04:08.717 --> 00:04:12.150
I'll pay three hundred pounds and not a penny more!"

58
00:04:12.151 --> 00:04:16.228
The judge trembled at Sir Richard's angry tone.

59
00:04:16.229 --> 00:04:20.731
"Please, gentlemen! Let's speak kindly to one another.

60
00:04:20.732 --> 00:04:24.028
There's no need to argue."

61
00:04:24.029 --> 00:04:27.611
Sir Richard motioned to one of his men to come forward.

62
00:04:27.612 --> 00:04:32.474
The biggest, strongest-looking man brought a leather bag to Sir Richard.

63
00:04:32.475 --> 00:04:38.543
The knight opened it and dumped a stream of gold coins onto the table in front of the abbot.

64
00:04:38.544 --> 00:04:46.002
"There, Abbot! I've paid my debt, and now I'm through with you!" Sir Richard turned and stormed away.

65
00:04:46.003 --> 00:04:50.115
Abbot Vincent was angry that he'd lost Sir Richard's property.

66
00:04:50.116 --> 00:04:53.127
He scowled at the sheriff.

67
00:04:53.128 --> 00:04:59.732
"Thanks to you, Sir Richard paid only three hundred pounds!"

68
00:04:59.733 --> 00:05:02.829
But the Sheriff of Nottingham wasn't listening.

69
00:05:02.830 --> 00:05:06.942
He was staring at the huge man who'd carried the gold.

70
00:05:06.943 --> 00:05:14.408
"Why, I know you—you're Reynold Greenleaf!" cried the sheriff. "My servant!"

71
00:05:14.409 --> 00:05:18.518
"Greetings, Sheriff!" Little John said with a grin.

72
00:05:18.519 --> 00:05:23.325
"I'll be sure to tell Robin Hood about the good deed you did today!"

73
00:05:23.326 --> 00:05:32.028
Then he turned and followed Sir Richard from the room, leaving the sheriff looking pale and stunned.

